        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I see.\r\n\r\nI don't think this is a good idea. Local session files are the way to use current directory specific sessions. Plus having current directory stored would not immediately prove useful for 'mini.sessions' itself, as there can be multiple sessions with the same current directory (hence, no guaranteed way to decide which session should be autoloaded).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
